ning, multi‑platform packaging and automated builds. Added Update Feed Publishing: Added build/update-publish.js that runs after signing and copies release artifacts ( .exe , .dmg , .zip , .AppImage , latest.yml ) to publish/desktop/ . The feed URL in package.json now points to https://neural-shell￾updates.yourdomain.com/desktop/ . Code Signing Stub: Added build/win-codesign.js . When the environment variables CSC_LINK and CSC_KEY_PASSWORD are absent, the script logs a warning and exits. When present, it can be extended to invoke the actual code signing tool. Documentation explaining certificate preparation and environment variables has been added to README.md . Cross‑Platform Packaging: Extended the Electron builder configuration to define build targets for macOS ( dmg , zip ) and Linux ( AppImage ). Added placeholder .icns and .png icons derived from the existing Windows .ico . Continuous Integration Pipeline: Added a GitHub Actions workflow .github/workflows/ release.yml that builds and tests the app on Windows, macOS and Ubuntu. The workflow installs dependencies, runs smoke tests, builds the app, publishes updates on Windows runners and uploads the resulting artifacts. Smoke Tests: Added a minimal test script under test/smoke.js and a corresponding npm run test:smoke command. The script ensures that key modules ( state , vaultEncryption , themeSwitcher , tierEngine , qrUnlock ) can be imported without error. This acts as a sanity check in CI environments where full UI testing is not possible. • • • • • 5 <PARSED TEXT FOR PAGE: 6 / 6> Installer Branding: Added build/installerHeader.bmp and set installerHeader and uninstallDisplayName properties in the NSIS configuration. This customises the Windows installer wizard header and uninstaller name. Changed Version Bump: Updated package.json version to 1.0.0 and added a test:smoke script. Added afterSign hook to invoke the update publishing script. Documentation: Expanded README.md with instructions on building installers, performing Windows code signing, and hosting update feeds. Removed Nothing was removed for this release. All previously implemented features (LLM streaming, QR unlock, AES‑GCM vault encryption, tier and rank effects, secure preload path, auto‑update events, diagnostic utilities and theme switching) remain intact and have been tested through the smoke test suite. • • • 6
